+
+## 5. Declared mover classes
+
+Reference, brand and theme token bytes (m02–m04) → `packages/tokens/dist/css/tokens.css` and every export (flat cssVariables, tailwind `tokens.json`, compose, ios-swift, ts), every component theme cell screenshot and contrast measurement, every chart SVG golden (paints and chrome colors), the 52-cell matrix rows, the certified matrix and its `tokenVersion`, the viz registry svgHash pins, the runtime sweep's chart-theme scopes and screenshots, `docs:check` surfaces quoting a hex or ratio, the `#1943` hue-revision and `#1850`/`#1863` dark-palette decisions (superseded by reason). Guardrail and validator changes (m01) → their contract specs. HC scope completion (m04) → `brands/*/hc.json` and the HC census only (no pixel claims this sprint).
+
+Non-movers: the semantic token key set; component implementation bytes and contracts; schemas and tool descriptions (unless a description quotes a color); the tool roster and ledger (24); the 17 saved-store hashes; object and trait definitions; runtime pass/fail semantics; the 13-row viz registry except `svgHash`/`contrast*`/`themes` fields.
+
+## 6. Descope ladder (in order; never past the never-cut line)
+
+1. The type/spacing/radius/elevation/focus pass carries (decision 12).
+2. m06 TraceLab pages reduce to one (Evidence ledger) with the reason.
+3. m04 categorical target 12 carries as a pinned ceiling ≥ 10 with the measured reason (never a caution pass).
+4. m04 HC scope narrows to the roles used by the four types that already render under HC plus chart chrome; the rest typed for Sprint 199 with the role list.
+5. m03 Brand B dark ships mechanically from the seed with no manual tuning pass.
+
+**Never cut:** frozen token names with the key-set pin; the generator with `--check`; the extended gates with the BEFORE red receipts; Brand A light and dark by design; one golden migration with attribution before update; the Subscription side-by-side; one capture; zero hand-edited token JSON; zero writes into TraceLab's repo; zero notices.
+
+## 7. Out of scope, carried by name
+
+HC pixel rendering of the nine deferred chart types → Sprint 199. Application craft (`#1832`, `#1881`, `#1915`) → Sprint 198. Chart residue (typed gaps, authoring-only patterns, bubble map, ECharts placement, soak, timezone) → Sprint 199. Brand source in the bundle, license, release → Sprint 200. `design.preview` from the bundle → Sprint 201. New semantic tokens, component API changes, Figma. Parts Town and mobile stay parked.
+
+## 8. Build and review
+
+- Worktree: `git worktree add ~/.codex/worktrees/s197/OODS-Forge -b codex/sprint-197-palette bc12723e9`; copy the four planning files from the primary checkout; `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, `pnpm build:tokens`, `pnpm build:packages`; commit the planning files first.
+- Gates by mission: `pnpm tokens-validate`, `pnpm check:tokens`, the tokens package build, `pnpm --filter @oods/viz-core test`, `pnpm --filter @oods/viz-render test`, `pnpm --filter @oods/mcp-server exec vitest run` (rebuild viz-core first: the mcp-server suite resolves `@oods/viz-core` to `dist`), `pnpm test:contrast`, `pnpm test:axe`, `pnpm docs:check`, the s193 runtime sweep (`scripts/product-reality/s193-runtime-cells.ts`) at close.
+- Golden migration: follow `artifacts/product-reality/sprint-195/m05/golden-migration/README.md` exactly (baseline → attribute → bounded `--update` with `--coverage.enabled=false` → matrix qualify/regenerate → attribution script); retain every initial red.
+- Capture: one five-suite capture under `#1833` in m07 (60 s budget, serial project for git-range specs, one isolated rerun for a lone timeout, never a full recapture). Root-core goes red under parallel scheduling; do not run suites concurrently. macOS has no `timeout`.
+- Receipts under `artifacts/product-reality/sprint-197/<mission>/`; the handoff at `m07/closeout/handoff.md`.
+- Review: a separate session; it opens by saying where we are in plain words (what works, what does not, what Derek can do with it today), inspects the m06 sheets before any gate, and decides genuine close. Sprint complete is the reviewing agent's call. After certification the reviewing agent fast-forwards the primary checkout, rebuilds, restarts `oods-forge-bridge`, and confirms `/health`; it deletes the primary's copies of the planning files after hash-checking them against the merged branch. No notices are prepared or sent.
